      "name": "Service disclosure",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Native expandable service diagnostics; shortened sample content.",
      "html": "<details class=\"ds-service\"><summary>Gitea<svg class=\"ds-chevron\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 5 7 7-7 7\"/></svg></summary><p>Git repositories and code collaboration.</p></details>",
      "css": ".ds-service{font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", sans-serif;padding:0 24px;border-radius:16px;background:var(--surface);color:var(--ink)}.ds-service summary{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;min-height:96px;list-style:none;cursor:pointer;font-size:15px;font-weight:600}.ds-service summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.ds-service summary:focus-visible { outline:3px solid var(--focus); outline-offset:4px; }.ds-chevron{width:17px;height:17px;fill:none;stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:1.7;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;transition:transform 160ms var(--ease)}.ds-service[open] .ds-chevron{transform:rotate(90deg)}.ds-service p{padding-bottom:24px;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-chevron{transition:none}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{transition:none!important;animation:none!important}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A quiet office home",
    "overview": "A quiet office home that reveals the next useful administrative task. Warm ivory, white surfaces, forest text, and muted green actions make a practical operating tool approachable. System sans typography supports readable diagnostics and familiar controls.\n\nThis system applies only to the experimental `/console` routes and `src-dashboard/assets/console.css`, with `console.html`, `console-icons.html`, and `console.js`. The legacy `dashboard.html` / `app.css` dark technical world is outside this scope. The console is a loopback-only, read-only preview behind a disabled-by-default flag; People and Shared folders explicitly remain not connected. This document records visual implementation, not production acceptance, authentication, or administration capabilities.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm neutral surfaces with forest actions.",
      "Task discovery followed by responsive full-page tools.",
      "Text-backed service state and expandable diagnostics."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The State Label Rule",
        "body": "Health color accompanies readable status text; color alone must not carry service state.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep these tokens scoped to the experimental console.",
      "Do pair health colors with readable state labels.",
      "Do retain the five mobile destinations and safe-area clearance."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't apply this palette to the legacy panel without a separate approved redesign.",
      "Don't present unconnected People or Shared folders as empty working administration.",
      "Don't replace full-page tools with movable windows."
    ]
  }
